# Security Best Practices

## Authentication
- API uses Hono and `@gafus/auth/jwt` for short-lived JWT access tokens and refresh sessions, not NextAuth.
- Browser clients use HttpOnly SameSite cookies; mobile clients use explicit Bearer tokens.
- Enforce role-based access control in API/route composition, never through untrusted client roles.

## Authorization and CSRF
- Every browser cookie mutation (`POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`) must pass strict trusted-Origin validation in the API (`apps/api/src/lib/browser-auth.ts`).
- Keep the Web browser Origin allowlist exact (`apps/api/src/middleware/cors.ts`), never enable wildcard cookie credentials.
- Native Bearer requests remain separately authenticated and must not require a browser Origin.
- Test the enforcement with `apps/api/src/middleware/cookie-origin-security.matrix.test.ts`.

## Input Validation
- Always validate with Zod schemas
- Sanitize user input
- Validate file uploads (type, size)
- Use parameterized queries (Prisma handles this)

## File Uploads
- Validate file type and size (e.g. video: type, max 100MB)
- Return clear error messages in Russian

## Environment Variables
- Never expose secrets to client
- Use `process.env` only in server code
- Validate env vars at startup
- Use `.env.local` for local development

## Cookie Consent

Согласие на cookies хранится в **localStorage** (ключ `gafus:cookieConsent:v1`), а не в cookies HTTP.

**Почему localStorage:**
- Не отправляется на сервер автоматически — меньше риск утечки и упрощение GDPR
- Достаточная персистентность для хранения выбора пользователя
- Отсутствие серверной логики — весь flow на клиенте

Компонент `CookieConsentBanner` и `resetCookieConsent` — из `@gafus/ui-components`. См. `docs/features/cookie-consent.md`.

## Best Practices
- Never trust client input
- Use HTTPS in production
- Implement rate limiting
- Log security events
- Keep dependencies updated
- Use Content Security Policy (CSP)
